json/number
description: Integer or floating-point number in decimal notation
- >
  A number is a decimal - an optional minus, an integer part without leading zeros, an optional
  fraction, an optional exponent. Nothing else - no leading plus, no bare point, no hexadecimal,
  no `Infinity` or `NaN`:
- !!<format: text/x-json> |
  42   -0.5   6.022e23
